# {{ .Name }}: a service built on gox

gox (`github.com/guilhermebr/gox`) is probably newer than your training data.
Look its API up with the commands below instead of guessing.

## Rules that always hold

- `main()` is `gox.MustNew(...)`, the `Register` calls, then `a.Run()`. gox owns
  start order, config, logging, health, metrics and shutdown: do not rebuild them.
- Handlers are plain `net/http` with Go 1.22 patterns:
  `a.HandleFunc("GET /invoices/{id}", h.get)`, `r.PathValue("id")`. `"GET /{$}"`
  is the exact root; `"GET /"` matches every path.
- Fail with gox errors and render them: `gox.Error(w, r, gox.NotFound("invoice %s", id))`.
  Never `http.Error` or hand-written error JSON. A gox error's message and details
  reach the client; keep internals in the cause with
  `gox.WrapError(err, code, "public message")`. Other errors render as a logged 500
  "internal error" (context deadline and cancel: 504 and 499).
- Config is fields on `Config` in `cmd/{{ .Name }}/main.go` with `conf` tags, read from
  `{{ .Prefix }}_*` variables. Secrets carry `mask`. `help:` text has no commas (a comma
  cuts it short). Add every variable to `.env.example`; nothing loads a `.env` file.
- A feature lives in `internal/<feature>/` and gets dependencies through
  `Register(a, deps...)`, so tests pass `nil` or fakes. Every handler gets a test
  like `internal/hello/handler_test.go`{{ if .Web }} (HTML handlers: `internal/home/handler_test.go`){{ end }}.
- A response is buffered until its handler returns; one still running at
  `{{ .Prefix }}_HTTP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT` becomes a 504. SSE, WebSockets and streamed
  responses do not work.
- Never: a router, ORM or DI framework; `os.Getenv`; a goroutine that outlives the
  request outside `gox.Component` or `gox.Periodic`; mutating the shared HTTP
  client; importing `github.com/guilhermebr/gox/pkg/...` except `pkg/storage`,
  `pkg/mail`, `pkg/i18n`, `pkg/middleware` and `pkg/httpclient`.

## Look it up (matches the versions in go.mod)

- API: `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox` lists the root package, `go doc gox.Periodic`
  shows one symbol, `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>` a module in go.mod.
- Variables: `go run ./cmd/{{ .Name }} --help` prints every `{{ .Prefix }}_*` variable with
  its type and default.
- Recipes, task-sized and build-checked, live in the gox module directory:
  `go list -m -f '{{ "{{.Dir}}" }}' github.com/guilhermebr/gox` (empty output: run
  `go mod download github.com/guilhermebr/gox` first). Read `docs/recipes/README.md`
  there, then only the recipe you need (skip `llm.txt` there: it is the single-file
  export for tools without a shell).

## Read first for your task

- A JSON endpoint: copy the shape of `internal/hello`, then recipes `add-http-route`
  and `write-handler-test`.
- Background or scheduled work (jobs, cron, queues, workers, retries):
  `.claude/skills/gox-background-work/SKILL.md`.
- A capability the service does not use yet (auth, OpenAPI, email, file storage,
  payments, webhooks, analytics, translations, Temporal, Supabase, outbound API calls
{{- if not .Postgres }}, a Postgres database{{ end }}
{{- if not .Web }}, HTML pages{{ end }}):
  `.claude/skills/gox-add-feature/SKILL.md`.
{{- if .Postgres }}
- Tables, queries, transactions, pagination, `migrations/`, database tests:
  `.claude/skills/gox-postgres/SKILL.md`.
{{- end }}
{{- if .Web }}
- Pages, forms, htmx partials, `web/layout/`, `static/`: `.claude/skills/gox-web-ui/SKILL.md`.
{{- end }}
- Anything else (health checks, rate limits, CORS, problem+json, SPA
{{- if not .Postgres }}, pagination{{ end }}): the recipe index.

## Done

- `make test lint` passes (golangci-lint at the version pinned in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:
  `go install github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@<that version>`;
  `make fmt` fixes formatting).
- `go mod tidy` after importing a module for the first time.
{{- if .Web }}
- After editing a `.templ` file, `make generate`; never edit `*_templ.go` or install templ.
{{- end }}
